{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured persistent TCP rsyslog forwarding for node2 `inventory` messages to `/var/log/inventory/node2.log` on node1. Verified delivery before and after restarting each node serially. The AlmaLinux release and kernel were unchanged.","actions_performed":["Configured node1 to receive TCP syslog on port 514 and persist only node2 `inventory` messages.","Added a permanent firewalld rule for TCP/514 on node1.","Configured node2 with an infinite-retry, disk-assisted rsyslog forwarding queue.","Validated both rsyslog configurations and verified live delivery.","Restarted node1 and node2 one at a time, confirming changed boot identities and complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Centralized inventory log delivery","command_ids":["cmd-e9d902388b714915","cmd-bce8d711eae04616","cmd-28a33fcd1ce54bad","cmd-45625896ef0546ea","cmd-9c5bbdc1c1c74dea"],"summary":"Configurations validated; node1 listened on TCP/514; the baseline inventory marker generated on node2 appeared in the required node1 file."},{"requirement":"Compatible installed platform retained","command_ids":["cmd-201139a44c23443c","cmd-f088582e88324cc1"],"summary":"Both nodes remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 and the installed rsyslog 8.2412 package."},{"requirement":"node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-fca4e661c3b34d03","cmd-5217958b0ce641da","cmd-3df6e28073f8402f","cmd-db1cb7c04dc8438c","cmd-6f9ec2290cea459e","cmd-582e9ba5d7054779"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from ea4e3fbd-2329-47e3-ad4f-e4f4d82214b7 to bf12c3ef-9e6c-4b4e-955e-abe2ec616215. Listener, firewall, existing data, and fresh log delivery recovered."},{"requirement":"node2 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-c9a56f13286d425f","cmd-51d2c5f35e0b44b9","cmd-ff3cecc56bb04b11","cmd-8e04ec82951e4dd8","cmd-712e8ac86a304045"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from f38484ef-a289-4d30-9a94-4ab42c44f900 to ed690699-17d5-438d-b8ee-7bdd57c9c176. rsyslog recovered enabled and active, configuration revalidated, and a new inventory message reached node1."}]}
